From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 11:58:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: enable HW GRO by default

The dynamic IFC code and the local-in offload steer a TCP flow of a
local application to an LRO ring, but the CDM LRO engine aggregates
only while rx-gro-hw is on, and a steered flow gets no gain without
it. No SmartOS component sets the feature, so it is now on from the
registration of every airoha net_device, for the LAN and the WAN
side. The wanted state of each QDMA starts as on too, so a
net_device and its QDMA agree before the first open. The first open
programs the engine, and ethtool can still turn the feature off.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c |    3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -1758,6 +1758,7 @@ static int airoha_qdma_init(struct platf
 	const char *res;
 
 	qdma->eth = eth;
+	qdma->hw_gro = true;
 	res = devm_kasprintf(eth->dev, GFP_KERNEL, "qdma%d", id);
 	if (!res)
 		return -ENOMEM;
@@ -4074,7 +4075,7 @@ static int airoha_alloc_gdm_device(struc
 	netdev->max_mtu = AIROHA_MAX_MTU;
 	netdev->watchdog_timeo = 5 * HZ;
 	netdev->hw_features = AIROHA_HW_FEATURES | NETIF_F_GRO_HW;
-	netdev->features |= AIROHA_HW_FEATURES;
+	netdev->features |= AIROHA_HW_FEATURES | NETIF_F_GRO_HW;
 	netdev->vlan_features = AIROHA_HW_FEATURES;
 	SET_NETDEV_DEV(netdev, eth->dev);
 
